    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1716" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Albĭnĭus</span></b> , ii,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a Roman</i> gens: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">C. Albinius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sest. 3, 6</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Albĭnĭānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to an Albinius.—Subst.</i>:
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Albĭnĭāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>adherents of Albinius</i>, <i><span class="en">Spart. Sev.
				10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tert. ad Scap.
		2</span></i>.</div>
